  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Basic Education Support Project in Khartoum State</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aiming to boys and girls from the most disadvantaged, poor and vulnerable communities have access to sustainable quality education in 7 schools in two localities - Oumbada and Karri- in Khartoum state. This could be done through set of activities include:
- Start up workshop/meeting
- Maintenance &amp; rehabilitation of 50 seating units (bench &amp; desk).
- Maintenance &amp; rehabilitation of 10 doors.
- Construction of school latrines in one school (6 rooms)
- Access to drinking water for 4 schools.
- Environmental awareness and Hygiene promotion campaigns.
- Provision of teaching &amp; learning materials for 8 schools.
- PTA training on school improvement plans (SIPs), Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR), child protection and accountability.
- Support 300 of grade 8 students in their national exams.
- M&amp;E and Lesson learning</narrative>
  </description>
